  "fused_kernel_explanation": "The fused / FlashAttention-style kernel never writes the S\u00d7S score matrix to HBM. It loads Q/K/V tiles into SRAM, computes local products, keeps a running softmax (m, l statistics) in on-chip memory, and writes only the output tile. That removes the O(S\u00b2) allocation that OOMs the naive path and the O(S\u00b2) memory traffic that makes naive attention bandwidth-bound."
